module tasks.`2026-11-20-test-process-leaks`

task TestProcessLeaks {
  title "Tests leak processes: orphaned supervisor/logic pairs, a Codex app-server daemon and landing-fixture cargo runs outlive their tests"
  verify $ make test-boundaries
  paths "crates/bboxy450-term", "crates/bbt-mux", "crates/bbt-supervisor", "scripts"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed.

    ## Evidence (2026-11-20, all ppid 1, killed by the Oracle by exact PID)
    - `target/debug/bboxy450-term supervisor` + `logic` from the ui-kit managed checkout, `HOME=$TMPDIR/.tmpOBex1e/home` (deleted), alive 15.5 h; they blocked `workspace_release` of the checkout.
    - `codex app-server daemon` + child from `/tmp/bbt-shared-codex-npclj1_4/home/.codex/...` (v0.166), alive 20 days.
    - Two `python … landing-fixture-*/.git/fixture-state/bin/cargo test -p c` runs, alive 25 days, fixture dirs deleted.

    ## Do
    Find each spawning test (real-process boundary tests, the shared-codex fixture, `scripts/test-landing.py` fixtures). Make each test own its children: process group plus kill-on-drop (or the existing test guard if one exists), so a panic or timeout cannot leave them behind. Add one broken control: a test that panics mid-run, followed by an assertion that no process carrying its temp HOME survives. Do not add a new reaper daemon.
    ## Root cause found for the `dq1-` leaks (Oracle, 2026-11-20 20:40)
    - Test: `crates/bboxy450-term/tests/dream_read.rs:57` (`tempfile` prefix `dq1-`) starts `--headless --ctl --unattended --test-account ... --run-dir <tmp>/run`. Its `Drop for Process` (`:120-141`) runs `ctl app stop` and kills only the app child; the detached supervisor survives whenever `app stop` does not reach it, reparents to PID 1 and outlives the deleted temp home. Six seen so far (5 from deleted worktrees, 1 from the inbox landing at 19:39, PID 14044).
    - **Fix direction:** the test owns the supervisor too: after `app stop`, read the supervisor PID from the private run dir (or ask `ctl app status`) and stop exactly that PID, then assert no process with the temp HOME remains. Prefer one shared test helper used by every real-process app test (dream_read, live, headless suites) rather than per-test copies.


    ## Report from seat:01M7ZVK9YFPRSBR7EJF6DPC5E1

    [[Verified]] make test-boundaries passed all 39 tests and both Dream Read process witnesses passed. The panic witness removed the private ctl endpoint, observed the live app and backend owners, then found zero processes carrying the fixture HOME. Shared Codex cleanup passed 10 tests and the landing deadline and FIFO controls passed three. The signed change removes frontend-only teardown, duplicate raw PID cleanup and the indefinite fake Cargo pause.

